# OpenAPI / Swagger

Google docstrings are for developers. `/docs` is the customer contract. Do not
let FastAPI or Pydantic dump a docstring into OpenAPI.

Routes: set `summary=`, `description=`, and `operation_id=` on the decorator.
Keep `name=` for `RouteLogger`. Public copy must not mention DI, loggers, or
kubelet rationale. Declare non-200 with `responses=`. Path params use
`Path(..., description=..., examples=...)`.

Models: `ConfigDict(json_schema_extra={"description": "..."})` overrides the
class docstring. Fields use `Field(description=..., examples=...)`. No ORM, no
"this model exists for OpenAPI". Leave FastAPI's `HTTPValidationError`.

`FastAPI(version=)` is `installed_app_version()`, not `ENV`.

Probes stay mounted; `include_in_schema` only when `ENV` is `local` or `dev`.
`/metrics` stays off the schema always.
